GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_RaceWeekend TO Formula1Backend.ApiUser;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_RaceWeekend TO Formula1Backend.DataAdmin;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_RaceSessions TO Formula1Backend.ApiUser;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_RaceSessions TO Formula1Backend.DataAdmin;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_Calendar TO Formula1Backend.ApiUser;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_Calendar TO Formula1Backend.DataAdmin;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_WeekendShape TO Formula1Backend.ApiUser;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_WeekendShape TO Formula1Backend.DataAdmin;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_LapChart TO Formula1Backend.ApiUser;
GRANT EXECUTE ON MICROFLOW Formula1Backend.Read_LapChart TO Formula1Backend.DataAdmin;

/*
 * The service grants live here because this is the file that declares the
 * service, and a service with no allowed role fails the build with CE0307
 * "At least one allowed role must be selected".
 *
 * They used to be a re-grant: `create or modify odata service` dropped role
 * access every time it rewrote a service, so any file modifying one had to put
 * the grants back or the next build broke. mxcli `715bac5` fixed the modelsdk
 * writer, which was the half `28ce821` missed, and a bare modify now preserves
 * them — verified. These stay because a fresh run still has to grant once.
 * FINDINGS §26, §41, §48.
 */
GRANT ACCESS ON ODATA SERVICE Formula1Backend.F1FanApi TO Formula1Backend.ApiUser;
GRANT ACCESS ON ODATA SERVICE Formula1Backend.F1FanApi TO Formula1Backend.DataAdmin;
